IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cor-dates`

-- Coroners Act 2008 (Vic) -- the rules the questions share: the s 3 definitions (senior next of kin, immediate family,
-- domestic partner, person placed in custody or care), the s 4 reportable death and the s 5 reviewable death, the
-- deaths that may leave the coronial system on natural causes (ss 17, 17A), the two duties with deadlines run as
-- regulative rules (ss 42(3) and 52(6)), and the Part 7 appeals table (who may appeal, the period, leave out of time,
-- appeals beyond a question of law).
--
-- This module holds the law that more than one question uses. The questions are asked in cor-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it;
-- where a section is used by one question only, the seat module applies its words there and cites them. Nothing here
-- is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "is not", "does not",
-- "must not", "is not required", "need not", "unless", "if" conditions that fail, a period the text fixes); or NOTHING
-- where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The coroner's and the courts'
-- judgments ("appears", "believes", "suspects", "satisfied", "considers", "sufficient interest", "appropriate",
-- "exceptional circumstances", "interests of justice") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Coroners Act
-- 2008, Version No. 046 (1 November 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the
-- authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the
-- Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Coroners Act 2008`

§§ `s 3 -- who the family are`

-- s 3(1) "senior next of kin" paragraphs (a) to (f) and "immediate family" name these relationships. "Parent, in
-- relation to a child, includes" a step-parent, adoptive or foster parent, guardian, or a person with custody or daily
-- care and control; "sibling ... includes a half-brother, half-sister, adoptive brother, adoptive sister, step-brother or
-- step-sister".
DECLARE `Relationship to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `spouse or domestic partner`
    `son or daughter`
    `parent`
    `sibling`
    `executor named in the will`
    `personal representative`
    `none of these`

-- s 3(1) "senior next of kin in relation to a deceased person, means -- (a) if the person, immediately before death had a
-- spouse or domestic partner -- the spouse or domestic partner; or (b) if the person immediately before death did not
-- have a spouse or domestic partner or if the spouse or domestic partner is not available -- a son or daughter of or over
-- the age of 18 years; or (c) if a spouse, domestic partner, son or daughter is not available -- a parent; or (d) ... --
-- a sibling who is of or over the age of 18 years; or (e) ... -- a person named in the will as an executor; or (f) ... --
-- a person who, immediately before the death, was a personal representative of the deceased; (g) ... -- a person
-- determined to be the senior next of kin under subsection (3)".
-- A "means" definition: FALSE where no paragraph applies. Paragraph (a) has no "available" condition (finding 1). "Son
-- or daughter" in (c) to (g) is read as one who qualifies under (b), of or over 18 (fork F1, finding 2).
GIVEN `my relationship`                         IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
      `I am 18 or over`                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `a spouse or domestic partner available`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult son or daughter available`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `a parent available`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult sibling available`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `an executor available`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `a personal representative available`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner determined me under s 3(3)`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- I am the senior next of kin` `my relationship` `I am 18 or over` `a spouse or domestic partner available` `an adult son or daughter available` `a parent available` `an adult sibling available` `an executor available` `a personal representative available` `the coroner determined me under s 3(3)` IF
        `paragraph (a)`
     OR `paragraph (b)`
     OR `paragraph (c)`
     OR `paragraph (d)`
     OR `paragraph (e)`
     OR `paragraph (f)`
     OR `paragraph (g)`
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS `my relationship` EQUALS `spouse or domestic partner`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS `my relationship` EQUALS `son or daughter` AND `I am 18 or over` AND (NOT `a spouse or domestic partner available`)
        `none of (a), (b)` MEANS (NOT `a spouse or domestic partner available`) AND (NOT `an adult son or daughter available`)
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS `my relationship` EQUALS `parent` AND `none of (a), (b)`
        `none of (a) to (c)` MEANS `none of (a), (b)` AND (NOT `a parent available`)
        `paragraph (d)` MEANS `my relationship` EQUALS `sibling` AND `I am 18 or over` AND `none of (a) to (c)`
        `none of (a) to (d)` MEANS `none of (a) to (c)` AND (NOT `an adult sibling available`)
        `paragraph (e)` MEANS `my relationship` EQUALS `executor named in the will` AND `none of (a) to (d)`
        `none of (a) to (e)` MEANS `none of (a) to (d)` AND (NOT `an executor available`)
        `paragraph (f)` MEANS `my relationship` EQUALS `personal representative` AND `none of (a) to (e)`
        `paragraph (g)` MEANS `the coroner determined me under s 3(3)` AND `none of (a) to (e)` AND (NOT `a personal representative available`)

-- s 3(1) "immediate family in relation to a deceased person, means spouse, domestic partner, son, daughter, parent,
-- sibling, executor, personal representative or a person determined to be the senior next of kin under subsection (3)".
-- A "means" definition; no age limit here.
GIVEN `my relationship` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`, `the coroner determined me under s 3(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- I am immediate family` `my relationship` `the coroner determined me under s 3(3)` IF
    (NOT (`my relationship` EQUALS `none of these`)) OR `the coroner determined me under s 3(3)`

-- s 3(1) "person placed in custody or care means -- (a) ... (l)" (paragraph (c) is repealed). Used by s 4(2)(c),
-- s 52(2)(b), s 67(2)(b)(i) and s 73(1B).
DECLARE `Custody or care` IS ONE OF
    `not in custody or care`
    `in the parental responsibility of the Secretary under the Children, Youth and Families Act 2005`
    `a child placed in emergency care under the Children, Youth and Families Act 2005`
    `under the control, care or custody of the Secretary to the Department of Human Services or of Health`
    `in the legal custody of the Secretary to the Department of Justice and Community Safety or the Chief Commissioner of Police`
    `in the custody of a police officer`
    `in the custody of a protective services officer`
    `detained in a treatment centre under the Severe Substance Dependence Treatment Act 2010`
    `a patient detained in a designated mental health service`
    `being taken into custody by a police officer or prison officer, or dying from injuries sustained then`
    `in Victoria and dying from an injury incurred while in the custody of the State`
    `a prescribed person or one of a prescribed class`

GIVEN c IS A `Custody or care`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- a person placed in custody or care` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `not in custody or care` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 4 -- reportable death`

-- The facts s 4 turns on. "death includes suspected death"; note 1 to the s 3 definition of "death": "A still-birth,
-- within the meaning of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1996, is not a death."
DECLARE `Death facts` HAS
    `the body is in Victoria`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the death occurred in Victoria`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cause of the death occurred in Victoria`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person ordinarily resided in Victoria`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was a still-birth`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it appears unexpected`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it appears unnatural or violent`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `it appears to result from an accident or injury`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `it occurred during a medical procedure`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `it followed a medical procedure and is or may be related`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a doctor would not have reasonably expected it`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the custody or care`                                           IS A `Custody or care`
    `the person was a mental health patient`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was under the Justice Secretary or a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was under a non-custodial supervision order`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the identity is unknown`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `no s 37(1) notice is signed or likely`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cause is not certified where it occurred, nor likely to be` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a prescribed class or circumstances`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `voluntary assisted dying in accordance with the 2017 Act`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4(1) "(a) the body is in Victoria; or (b) the death occurred in Victoria; or (c) the cause of the death occurred in
-- Victoria; or (d) the person ordinarily resided in Victoria at the time of death".
GIVEN f IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(1) -- the death is connected with Victoria` f IF
        f's `the body is in Victoria`
     OR f's `the death occurred in Victoria`
     OR f's `the cause of the death occurred in Victoria`
     OR f's `the person ordinarily resided in Victoria`

-- s 4(2)(a) "a death that appears to have been unexpected, unnatural or violent or to have resulted, directly or
-- indirectly, from an accident or injury", without the "unexpected" limb (ss 17(1)(a) and 17A(1)(a)(i) set it apart).
GIVEN f IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(2)(a) -- other than unexpected` f IF
    f's `it appears unnatural or violent` OR f's `it appears to result from an accident or injury`

-- s 4(2)(b) "a death that occurs -- (i) during a medical procedure; or (ii) following a medical procedure where the death
-- is or may be causally related to the medical procedure -- and a registered medical practitioner would not, immediately
-- before the procedure was undertaken, have reasonably expected the death".
GIVEN f IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(2)(b) -- a medical procedure death` f IF
        `the death occurred in or after the procedure`
    AND f's `a doctor would not have reasonably expected it`
    WHERE
        `the death occurred in or after the procedure` MEANS
            f's `it occurred during a medical procedure` OR f's `it followed a medical procedure and is or may be related`

-- s 4(2)(b), (c), (d), (e), (f), (g) and (j): the heads ss 17(1)(ab) and 17A(1)(a) rule out.
GIVEN f IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(2)(b) to (g) or (j)` f IF
        `s 4(2)(b) -- a medical procedure death` f
     OR `s 3 -- a person placed in custody or care` (f's `the custody or care`)
     OR f's `the person was a mental health patient`
     OR f's `the person was under the Justice Secretary or a police officer`
     OR f's `the person was under a non-custodial supervision order`
     OR f's `the identity is unknown`
     OR f's `a prescribed class or circumstances`

-- s 4(2)(h) "a death that occurs in Victoria if a notice under section 37(1) of the Births, Deaths and Marriages
-- Registration Act 1996 has not been signed and is not likely to be signed".
GIVEN f IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(2)(h)` f IF f's `the death occurred in Victoria` AND f's `no s 37(1) notice is signed or likely`

-- s 4(2)(i) "a death that occurs at a place outside Victoria if the cause of death is not certified by a person who,
-- under the law in force in that place, is authorised to certify that death and the cause of death is not likely to be
-- certified by a person who is authorised to certify in that place".
GIVEN f IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(2)(i)` f IF (NOT f's `the death occurred in Victoria`) AND f's `the cause is not certified where it occurred, nor likely to be`

-- s 4(2): "the deaths are -- (a) ... (j)". A closed list.
GIVEN f IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(2) -- a death of a listed kind` f IF
        f's `it appears unexpected`
     OR `s 4(2)(a) -- other than unexpected` f
     OR `s 4(2)(b) to (g) or (j)` f
     OR `s 4(2)(h)` f
     OR `s 4(2)(i)` f

-- s 4(1) "a death of a person is a reportable death if -- (a) ... (d) -- and the death was a death specified in
-- subsection (2)"; s 4(3) "Despite subsection (2), the death of a person who has been administered or self-administered a
-- voluntary assisted dying substance ... in accordance with that Act is not a reportable death." A still-birth is not a
-- death (note 1 to s 3; fork F2).
GIVEN f IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 -- a reportable death` f IF
        (NOT f's `it was a still-birth`)
    AND (NOT f's `voluntary assisted dying in accordance with the 2017 Act`)
    AND `s 4(1) -- the death is connected with Victoria` f
    AND `s 4(2) -- a death of a listed kind` f

-- ss 17(1)(a), (ab) and 17A(1)(a): a reportable death that is reportable "only because -- (i) it is unexpected; or (ii)
-- it is referred to in section 4(2)(h); or (iii) it is referred to in section 4(2)(i)". s 17(1)(a) and (ab) describe the
-- same deaths by excluding the other heads (finding 4).
GIVEN f IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 17, 17A -- reportable only because unexpected, (h) or (i)` f IF
        `s 4 -- a reportable death` f
    AND (NOT `s 4(2)(a) -- other than unexpected` f)
    AND (NOT `s 4(2)(b) to (g) or (j)` f)

§§ `s 5 -- reviewable death`

-- s 5(1) "the death of a child (the deceased child) is a reviewable death if the deceased child is the second or
-- subsequent child of the deceased child's parent to have died and one of the following applies -- (a) ... (d)";
-- (2) "Despite subsection (1), a death of a deceased child is not a reviewable death if -- (a) the death occurs in a
-- hospital; and (b) the child was born at a hospital and had always been an in-patient of a hospital; and (c) the death is
-- not a reportable death." s 3: "child means a person under the age of 18 years".
GIVEN f                                        IS A `Death facts`
      `the deceased was under 18`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `a second or later child of a parent to die` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the death occurred in a hospital`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `born at a hospital and always an in-patient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5 -- a reviewable death` f `the deceased was under 18` `a second or later child of a parent to die` `the death occurred in a hospital` `born at a hospital and always an in-patient` IF
        (NOT f's `it was a still-birth`)
    AND `the deceased was under 18`
    AND `a second or later child of a parent to die`
    AND `s 4(1) -- the death is connected with Victoria` f
    AND (NOT (`the death occurred in a hospital` AND `born at a hospital and always an in-patient` AND (NOT `s 4 -- a reportable death` f)))

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open`

-- s 52(6): "Within 3 months of receiving a request under subsection (5), the coroner must, in writing, advise the person
-- who made the request that the coroner has -- (a) decided to hold an inquest; or (b) decided that an inquest will not be
-- held; or (c) not made a decision ... and that the coroner will advise the person of the decision when the decision has
-- been made." s 53(3) is the same for a fire. Encoded for what the person must be given, by when. Days from receipt.
DECLARE `Coroner` IS ONE OF
    `the coroner`

DECLARE `Coroner's act` IS ONE OF
    `advise the requester in writing where the inquest decision stands`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Coroner` `Coroner's act`
`s 52(6) -- the coroner must answer the request for an inquest` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the coroner`
    MUST `advise the requester in writing where the inquest decision stands`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the coroner` BECAUSE "the coroner did not advise in writing, within 3 months of receiving the request, that an inquest will be held, will not be held, or is not yet decided (s 52(6), s 53(3))"

-- The helper that runs the duty over what happened (in the shape of the Civil Procedure Act 2010 encoding's helper). On
-- the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED means in
-- time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it now would still be in time. It takes
-- a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule`                    IS A DEONTIC `Coroner` `Coroner's act`
      `the act has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done`   IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`                IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of the coroner's duty` `the rule` `the act has been done` `the time the act was done` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the coroner` `advise the requester in writing where the inquest decision stands` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the coroner` `advise the requester in writing where the inquest decision stands` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

-- s 52(6) by dates: the last day is the day 3 months after the day the coroner received the request (fork F3).
GIVEN `the day the request was received` IS A DATE
      `the coroner has advised`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the coroner advised`      IS A DATE
      `today`                            IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`s 52(6) -- what became of the coroner's answer` `the day the request was received` `the coroner has advised` `the day the coroner advised` `today` MEANS
    `what became of the coroner's duty` (`s 52(6) -- the coroner must answer the request for an inquest` (`the days from` `the day the request was received` `to` (`the date` 3 `months after` `the day the request was received`))) `the coroner has advised` (`the days from` `the day the request was received` `to` `the day the coroner advised`) (`the days from` `the day the request was received` `to` `today`)

-- s 42(3): "A person who is required to give a document or prepared statement to the coroner under subsection (1) must
-- not, without a lawful excuse, fail to comply with the requirement within the period specified by the coroner. 20
-- penalty units." s 42(2)(b): the requirement must "specify a reasonable period of time for compliance"; the period is
-- counted from service (s 42(2)(c)), and its last day is asked.
DECLARE `Person required` IS ONE OF
    `the person required`

DECLARE `Required act` IS ONE OF
    `give the coroner the document or prepared statement`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person required` `Required act`
`s 42(3) -- I must comply with the coroner's requirement` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the person required`
    MUST `give the coroner the document or prepared statement`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person required` BECAUSE "the document or prepared statement was not given within the period the coroner specified; without a lawful excuse this is an offence, 20 penalty units (s 42(3))"

GIVEN `the rule`                    IS A DEONTIC `Person required` `Required act`
      `the act has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done`   IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`                IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of my requirement` `the rule` `the act has been done` `the time the act was done` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the person required` `give the coroner the document or prepared statement` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the person required` `give the coroner the document or prepared statement` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

GIVEN `the day I was served`         IS A DATE
      `the last day allowed`         IS A DATE
      `I have complied`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I complied`           IS A DATE
      `today`                        IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`s 42(3) -- what became of my compliance` `the day I was served` `the last day allowed` `I have complied` `the day I complied` `today` MEANS
    `what became of my requirement` (`s 42(3) -- I must comply with the coroner's requirement` (`the days from` `the day I was served` `to` `the last day allowed`)) `I have complied` (`the days from` `the day I was served` `to` `the day I complied`) (`the days from` `the day I was served` `to` `today`)

§§ `Part 7 -- appeals to the Supreme Court`

DECLARE `Decision appealed` IS ONE OF
    `a determination that the death is not a reportable death (s 78)`
    `a direction that an autopsy be performed (s 79(1))`
    `a refusal to direct an autopsy (s 79(3))`
    `a determination not to investigate a fire (s 80)`
    `an authorisation of an exhumation (s 81(1))`
    `a refusal to authorise an exhumation (s 81(3))`
    `a determination not to hold an inquest (s 82)`
    `the findings of a coroner (s 83)`
    `a refusal to set aside findings or re-open an investigation (s 84)`
    `a refusal to re-open a discontinued investigation (s 84A)`
    `an order releasing a body, or its terms (s 85)`

-- Who may appeal: ss 78(1), 79(1), (3), 80(1), 81(1), (3), 82(1), 83(1), (2), 84(1), 84A(1), 85(1). Each grant is
-- limited by its own wording, so a person outside it gets NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*. s 83(1) "a person
-- with a sufficient interest in an investigation may appeal against the findings ... after an investigation" is read to
-- cover findings after an inquest too (fork F5).
DECLARE `My part in the decision` HAS
    `I reported the death`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the senior next of kin`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I made the request or application decided`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was notified of the exhumation authorisation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have a sufficient interest`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was an interested party at the inquest`        IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN d IS A `Decision appealed`, p IS A `My part in the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 7 -- I may appeal` d p MEANS
    IF `standing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `standing` MEANS
            CONSIDER d
            WHEN `a determination that the death is not a reportable death (s 78)` THEN p's `I reported the death`
            WHEN `a direction that an autopsy be performed (s 79(1))` THEN p's `I am the senior next of kin`
            WHEN `a refusal to direct an autopsy (s 79(3))` THEN p's `I am the senior next of kin` OR p's `I made the request or application decided`
            WHEN `a determination not to investigate a fire (s 80)` THEN p's `I made the request or application decided`
            WHEN `an authorisation of an exhumation (s 81(1))` THEN p's `I am the senior next of kin` OR p's `I was notified of the exhumation authorisation`
            WHEN `a refusal to authorise an exhumation (s 81(3))` THEN p's `I made the request or application decided`
            WHEN `a determination not to hold an inquest (s 82)` THEN p's `I made the request or application decided`
            WHEN `the findings of a coroner (s 83)` THEN p's `I have a sufficient interest` OR p's `I was an interested party at the inquest`
            WHEN `a refusal to set aside findings or re-open an investigation (s 84)` THEN p's `I made the request or application decided`
            WHEN `a refusal to re-open a discontinued investigation (s 84A)` THEN p's `I made the request or application decided`
            WHEN `an order releasing a body, or its terms (s 85)` THEN p's `I made the request or application decided`

-- The period, where it is counted in days or months: ss 78(2), 80(2) "within 28 days after the day on which the
-- determination of the coroner is made"; 81(4) "within 3 months after the refusal"; 82(2) "within 3 months after the day
-- on which the determination of the coroner is made"; 83(3) "within 6 months after the day ..."; 84(2), 84A(2) "within
-- 90 days after the refusal". The hour periods (ss 79(4), 81(2), 85(2)) and "before the direction takes effect"
-- (s 79(2)) are asked in hours by their own questions: NOTHING here, kind *limited by its own wording* (no last day).
GIVEN d IS A `Decision appealed`, `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Part 7 -- the last day to appeal` d `the day of the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `a determination that the death is not a reportable death (s 78)` THEN JUST (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the decision`)
    WHEN `a determination not to investigate a fire (s 80)` THEN JUST (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the decision`)
    WHEN `a refusal to authorise an exhumation (s 81(3))` THEN JUST (`the date` 3 `months after` `the day of the decision`)
    WHEN `a determination not to hold an inquest (s 82)` THEN JUST (`the date` 3 `months after` `the day of the decision`)
    WHEN `the findings of a coroner (s 83)` THEN JUST (`the date` 6 `months after` `the day of the decision`)
    WHEN `a refusal to set aside findings or re-open an investigation (s 84)` THEN JUST (`the date` 90 `days after` `the day of the decision`)
    WHEN `a refusal to re-open a discontinued investigation (s 84A)` THEN JUST (`the date` 90 `days after` `the day of the decision`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 86: "The Supreme Court may grant leave to appeal out of time under section 78, 80, 81(3), 82, 83, 84 or 84A if the
-- Supreme Court -- (a) is of the opinion that the failure to institute the appeal within the specified period was due to
-- exceptional circumstances; and (b) is satisfied that granting the leave is desirable in the interests of justice."
GIVEN d IS A `Decision appealed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86 -- leave out of time is available for` d IF
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `a direction that an autopsy be performed (s 79(1))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a refusal to direct an autopsy (s 79(3))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an authorisation of an exhumation (s 81(1))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order releasing a body, or its terms (s 85)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
